1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,707
Mandate Wallet lets an AI agent purchase
an approved API service within an

2
00:00:05,707 --> 00:00:10,976
owner-defined budget. We will connect it
to Claude Desktop, obtain an ETH

3
00:00:10,976 --> 00:00:15,805
statistics sample, and produce a short
brief. The transactions in this

4
00:00:15,805 --> 00:00:18,000
demonstration run on Base Sepolia.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,800
Claude Desktop is signed in, the Mandate
source component is running, and

6
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:28,400
the owner wallet has test ETH and test
USDC. These are testnet assets. The

7
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,400
API and payment facilitator are controlled
demonstration services, and the

8
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,000
statistics are fixed samples.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:41,059
Choose Testnet and Base Sepolia in the
setup wizard. Connect the owner

10
00:00:41,059 --> 00:00:46,941
wallet, then review deployment, funding
and permissions. We transfer zero

11
00:00:46,941 --> 00:00:54,588
point one five test USDC to the smart
account and fund operator gas

12
00:00:54,588 --> 00:01:02,235
separately. The task budget is zero point
one five, each payment is capped

13
00:01:02,235 --> 00:01:09,882
at zero point one, and the session expires
after one hour. The owner

14
00:01:09,882 --> 00:01:14,000
confirms these transactions in the
external wallet.

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,789
After confirmation, open the authorization
transaction in BaseScan. Check

16
00:01:17,789 --> 00:01:22,000
the Base Sepolia network, transaction hash
and successful receipt. The

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,053
contract log links the session to the
approved mandate. The complete hash

18
00:01:27,053 --> 00:01:30,000
will also appear in our execution
evidence.

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,370
Download the Guided package for this Base
Sepolia configuration. In Claude

20
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:45,978
Desktop, open Settings, Extensions and
Advanced settings, then import and

21
00:01:45,978 --> 00:01:55,109
enable the package. Its local connection
is already configured, so no Agent

22
00:01:55,109 --> 00:02:04,239
profile or Connection file is selected.
Start a new conversation using this

23
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:05,000
connection.

24
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,810
Ask Claude to read the account context and
quote the approved ETH sample

25
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:17,048
without purchasing. Check the chain,
account, active session and remaining

26
00:02:17,048 --> 00:02:23,333
budget. The sample costs zero point zero
one test USDC. Installing the

27
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:27,000
connector does not expand the approved
authority.

28
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,188
Authorize the quoted purchase. Mandate
registers the commitment before

29
00:02:33,188 --> 00:02:40,750
releasing a payment signature. The USDC
transfer settles on Base Sepolia,

30
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:47,625
but our controlled service deliberately
fails its first response. Claude

31
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:53,812
reports payment, delivery and result
validation separately. A successful

32
00:02:53,812 --> 00:03:00,000
payment alone does not mean the data was
delivered.

33
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,261
Open the settlement transaction in
BaseScan. Check Success, the test USDC

34
00:03:05,261 --> 00:03:11,000
contract, and the ERC-twenty transfer from
the smart account to the approved

35
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:17,217
recipient for zero point zero one USDC.
The transaction sender may be the

36
00:03:17,217 --> 00:03:21,522
facilitator paying gas; the token-transfer
sender identifies the paying

37
00:03:21,522 --> 00:03:22,000
account.

38
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,898
Ask Claude to retry the same ETH step. The
original order and settlement

39
00:03:28,898 --> 00:03:35,796
hash are retained, and there is no second
payment. The service returns the

40
00:03:35,796 --> 00:03:42,163
sample and the result checker validates
it. Claude then writes a brief,

41
00:03:42,163 --> 00:03:48,000
labels the data as a demonstration sample,
and cites the receipt.

42
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:54,632
The owner now revokes this session through
the wallet workspace and confirms

43
00:03:54,632 --> 00:04:01,263
the transaction in the external wallet.
Open the resulting BaseScan page and

44
00:04:01,263 --> 00:04:06,789
inspect the SessionRevoked log. This
changes future spending authority while

45
00:04:06,789 --> 00:04:09,000
preserving the completed purchase.

46
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:15,545
Finally, ask Claude to attempt the unused
BTC sample. The revoked session

47
00:04:15,545 --> 00:04:21,545
prevents a new payment registration. This
refusal has no new transaction

48
00:04:21,545 --> 00:04:28,091
hash because it is stopped before
broadcast. We retain the tool result,

49
00:04:28,091 --> 00:04:33,000
permission state and unchanged payment
records as refusal evidence.

50
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:37,722
The evidence package connects each
recorded step to its transaction,

51
00:04:37,722 --> 00:04:42,444
contract events and service outcome.
Payment and service delivery are

52
00:04:42,444 --> 00:04:47,167
documented separately. A local practice
option is also available for

53
00:04:47,167 --> 00:04:50,000
learning the workflow without public-
testnet funds.
